between the respondent referred, P&DD, and AKHSP.
At the end of each questionnaire, respondents were invited to provide verbal consent to participate in a follow-
up survey conducted via phone. They were informed that participation was entirely voluntary, that their
information would remain anonymous, and that they had the right to withdraw at any time. If consent was
granted, respondents were asked to provide their personal or the household’s shared phone number, with the
explicit instruction not to share phone numbers belonging to other household members or individuals outside
their household.
2.6  PROTOCOL PROTECTION AND ETHICS REVIEW
