As part of the informed consent process, all respondents were informed about the purpose of the survey, that
participation was voluntary, their responses would remain confidential and anonymous,  and they had the right
to refuse to answer any questions or to stop the interview at any time. Consent scripts for children were written
in Urdu that was age-appropriate and easy for them to understand.
